{"id": "EUVD-2026-76629", "enisaUuid": "67c6d42b-ba47-347a-a156-bc5f1f135957", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nzram: set default primary compressor in zram_destroy_comps()\n\nPatch series \"zram: fix zram issues reported by sashiko\".\n\nSashiko drove by and reported [1] a couple of zram issues:\na possible BUG_ON() in zlib code due to missing winbits range\nvalidation and one possible NULL-ptr dereference in zcomp.\nBoth are low risk yet still worth fixing.\n\n\nThis patch (of 2):\n\nzram_destroy_comps() resets all compressors and leaves them set to NULL,\nincluding the primary one, which is invalid device state, as now\ncomp_algorithm_show()->strcmp() can be called on a NULL compressor.  Set\ndefault primary compressor in zram_destroy_comps().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5fda7def04d98ab7c5cbb2394714fb1f8c56cb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bf3328eeec9afc2a55632ff47fc18101ea62d73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cec3e60e9f2d1324179df3aa91656f90095cf8f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dea8f13c3dfad8b990f8ea96c997aabeebbc1d22", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dde75313eed0b014c437f48dd75c0308b592cbf9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5wpf-6ffc-hwm4", "CVE-2026-89717"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "030c531c-83cf-3f15-9208-18074b902632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "486fd58af7ac1098b68370b1d4d9f94a2a1c7124 <dde75313eed0b014c437f48dd75c0308b592cbf9"}, {"id": "1c2bfadf-b857-3242-ab03-7fcb0351a36b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "486fd58af7ac1098b68370b1d4d9f94a2a1c7124 <dea8f13c3dfad8b990f8ea96c997aabeebbc1d22"}, {"id": "30b5d067-a797-34b7-aba3-3028fcb7e01b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "32a9ca33-9503